{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: pi-durable Workers AI default at 12494f3eef37088c2f995b0295229134da9bc9ac, on all 12 artifacts with notes/2026-10-01-pi-durable.md first. This satisfies the provider change in request 2284c958, within the existing standalone spike. Full production runtime request fa6d295a remains open.\n\nArchitecture: Workers AI is the explicit live default, using the Worker's AI binding without a model key. The adapter reuses pi-ai's catalog and chat-completions streaming client; it forwards model inputs and raw responses without manufacturing tool outcomes. Agent registration uses the same path that the provider tests exercise. REST Workers AI requires both account and API token; OpenRouter remains configurable. Scripted tests stay offline. The binding catalog includes older models whose response shape needs conversion; README states that limitation. The chosen GLM-4.7-Flash supports the spike's multi-turn tools and OpenAI-shaped stream. Cloudflare's current model page confirms 131,072 context and USD 0.0605/M input, USD 0.40/M output (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/glm-4.7-flash/).\n\nSecurity: The default removes a model credential from the agent. Alternative credentials enter an in-memory store, not SQLite or process.env, and test configuration passes only the selected provider's variables. REST permissions match Cloudflare's guidance: Workers AI Read and Workers AI Edit, scoped to the intended account (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/get-started/rest-api/). No new credentials, deployments or live inference were performed by checker. The delegate key, viewer/steerer authorization and other production custody obligations remain in fa6d295a. Raw-response and signal handling agree with the official binding implementation (https://github.com/cloudflare/workerd/blob/main/src/cloudflare/internal/ai-api.ts).\n\nSimplification: This is a small adapter around the pinned provider/client rather than another streaming parser. Provider selection has one shared module for host configuration and workerd tests; missing credentials fail an explicitly requested live run instead of silently skipping. The three provider paths remain distinct and inspectable.\n\nValidation: Fresh detached checkout, independent standalone npm ci (185 packages), pinned vendor extraction, 68 offline workerd tests passed and one live test skipped; strict spike sources have no type errors with exactly all seven previously reviewed vendor diagnostics; check:test passed all eight positive/negative gate cases. No root node_modules was needed. Four independent workerd controls against the actual adapter/client passed: raw 429, thrown binding transport failure, truncated SSE without finish reason and cancellation forwarded to the binding. The first diagnostic run expected the transport exception's original wording; the SDK correctly normalizes it to Connection error. Correcting that diagnostic expectation gave four passes, with no candidate edit. Initial baseline attempts before vendor extraction were setup failures and are not reported as candidate failures. Diagnostic source/logs are in /tmp/artroom-checker-pi-workersai-diagnostics and /tmp/artroom-checker-pi-workersai-failures.log; candidate worktree is clean. All 12 changed paths match the artifact set; unchanged spike/note bytes were credited to the prior reviewed pi head 8306d426 and base 3f44c993.\n\nDated evidence: Reviewed all 22 rows in results/live-runs-2026-10-02.txt and the complete final SPIKE-LIVE JSON. Binding path: 19/20 passed, USD about 0.0073 total by the catalog price table; REST and OpenRouter passed once each. Final recorded binding run has one injected reset after propose, two Agent opens, exactly one prepared send/admission each for claim/propose/land, no refusals, accepted when answered and landed after the Room alarm, mainIsHead true, 1,606 input/471 output tokens, USD 0.000285563. This runs the real pinned Room through a service binding with fake Artifacts and simulated workspace pushing; it is not a deployed production/Git credential proof. The account invoice was not read, and checker did not reproduce live inference.\n\nFollow-up, without scope reduction: Run 5 ended on an empty model turn after propose, leaving a proposal open and no land. The notes disclose it rather than claiming universal success. Production must use durable task-completion checks and attention/alarm recovery to reach a terminal Room outcome or report why it cannot, including empty/error turns and model outages. Nine successful runs chose all four tools before seeing the claim result; ordered execution worked for this fixed task, but production tools must revalidate prerequisites and authority after every result. A model override from the older response-shape catalog needs conversion or a clear refusal before use. Keep the production runtime, distinct identities, real workspace/CAS path, revocation/adversarial tests and secret custody in fa6d295a; this approval closes none of those obligations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:630e006eea7fd58f3daab6590950271d45b13acd","binding":"assigned","head":"12494f3eef37088c2f995b0295229134da9bc9ac","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1c21eae8c1d96cbdcfa46f9358b6407fa66dcd66\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:447eba18de09f821eadd23a7829e45b1c0ddbb44\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:afc01577a791bc7aab70e8fe22eefd902d08ff50","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}